Input: {"question": "Who is the director of the film \"Game of Death\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d00", "start": 0, "end": 183, "text": "13 Beloved 13 Beloved ( or \"13 Game Sayong\", also 13: Game of Death) is a 2006 Thai horror comedy film written and directed by Chukiat Sakveerakul and starring Krissada Sukosol Clapp."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d00", "start": 184, "end": 447, "text": "The story, about a man who is led through progressively challenging, degrading, and dangerous stunts by mysterious callers from an underground reality game show, is adapted from the \"13th Quiz Show\" episode in the \"My Mania\" comic-book series by Eakasit Thairaat."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d00", "start": 448, "end": 547, "text": "It was the second feature-length film for Chukiat, who previously directed the horror film \"Pisaj\"."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d00", "start": 548, "end": 612, "text": "The film won several awards in Thailand and from film festivals."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d00", "start": 613, "end": 619, "text": "Remake"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d01", "start": 0, "end": 205, "text": "Game of Death II Game of Death II (, aka Tower of Death and The New Game of Death) is a 1981 Hong Kong martial arts film directed by Ng See-yuen starring Bruce Lee, Tong Lung, Huong Cheng Li and Roy Horan."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d01", "start": 206, "end": 311, "text": "This film was marketed as a sequel to Bruce Lee's last and only partially completed film \"Game of Death\"."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d01", "start": 312, "end": 470, "text": "Bruce Lee died some years before the production of \"Game of Death II\" and most of his scenes are taken from Lee's older films; mostly from \"Enter the Dragon\"."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d01", "start": 471, "end": 534, "text": "Aside from the International English dub giving the \"Bruce Lee\""}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d02", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "of these films pre-dated Robert Clouse 's official Game of Death ( 1978 ) ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d02", "start": 76, "end": 95, "text": "The Game of Death !"}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d02", "start": 96, "end": 441, "text": "( 1974 ) Goodbye Bruce Lee : His Last Game of Death ( 1975 ) Enter the Game of Death ( 1978 ) The True Game of Death ( 1979 ) Game of Death II ( Tower of Death ) ( 1981 ) Clouse 's film had a sequel in 1981 , Game of Death II , a kung fu action mystery film directed by Ng See-yuen which used cut footage from Lee 's Enter the Dragon to have him"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "some nifty pugilism\"."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 22, "end": 145, "text": "Jamie Russell of \"Total Film\" rated it 2/5 stars and called it \"your standard CIA-Mafia-doublecrossing-flashback-nonsense\"."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 146, "end": 314, "text": "Game of Death (2010 film) Game of Death is a 2010 American action film directed by Giorgio Serafini, and starring Wesley Snipes, Zoë Bell, Gary Daniels and Robert Davi."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 315, "end": 396, "text": "The film was released on direct-to-DVD in the United States on February 15, 2011."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 397, "end": 428, "text": "The story is told in flashback."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 429, "end": 528, "text": "CIA agent Marcus Jones recounts his final mission in the form of a confession to a Catholic priest."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d03", "start": 529, "end": 615, "text": "The mission begins when Jones's mentor in the CIA, Dietrich, informs him that his next"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d04", "start": 0, "end": 569, "text": "IMDbPro IMDb RATING 4.7 / 10 7.2K YOUR RATING Rate Director Giorgio Serafini Writers Jim Agnew Megan Brown Martinez Stars Wesley Snipes Aunjanue Ellis-Taylor Zoë Bell 36 User reviews 43 Critic reviews See production info at IMDbPro Top cast 61 Edit Wesley Snipes Marcus Aunjanue Ellis-Taylor Rachel ( as Aunjanue Ellis ) Zoë Bell Floria ( as Zoe Bell ) Ernie Hudson Clarence Quinn Duffy Redvale Gary Daniels Zander Robert Davi Smith Eyad Elbitar Driver Simon Rhee Agent # 1 Ho-Sung Pak Agent # 2 … Efka Kvaraciejus Agent # 4 Carl Anthony Nespoli Agent # 4 … Don Richard"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d05", "start": 0, "end": 54, "text": "and the head of the hedge fund that is financing him ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d05", "start": 55, "end": 147, "text": "His CIA backup has other plans and turns on him and it 's a fight to survive in a hospital ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d05", "start": 148, "end": 272, "text": "Secret Ops agent Marcus is sent to Detroit to take out an arms dealer and the head of the hedge fund that is financing him ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60fd7fd4400:d05", "start": 273, "end": 365, "text": "His CIA backup has other plans and turns on him and it 's a fight to survive in a hospital ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0419-c60f